            <ArticleTitle>[Prevalence of asthma in schoolchildren from the Mexican city Hermosillo].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>397-401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Asthma is a very common disease, but its prevalence greatly varies from region to region, even in the same country. In the northwest of Mexico there is a lack of epidemiological studies on this disease. In this work a standardized questionnaire (ISAAC) was applied to parents of children attending 8 primary schools in the Mexican city of Hermosillo, Sonora. Of 3000 questionnaires sent, 1489 (49%) were acceptably answered. Children were of either sex and 9.1 +/- 1.8 years old (mean +/- SD). From this population, 74 (10.4%) out of 713 male and 67 (8.6%) out of 776 female children had an affirmative response to que question &quot;Have you ever had asthma?&quot;, from which we conclude that global prevalence of asthma in the studied sample was 9.5%, an intermediate figure among those reported from other studies performed in Mexico.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
